    "notes": "Fix of KG-2026-11-20-a, which failed QA again on a 5.0 s shot (limit 5) after the first fix split only the twist and button shots. This time every two-line shot is split, so each line gets its own shot (19 shots, one line each, hold 0.1) and no shot can hold more than one line plus a short pause. The chip now moves on the punch shot itself (BALCONY: 1, 2, 3 lands as Tanya says 'Balcony!'), which also helps the mute test. Words, voices and pace 28 unchanged, so pace and length stay as they passed (adds about 0.4 s). Type stays door-arrivals because this is a fix of a needs-fix reel, which the routine puts before any new idea. Original notes: last 4 gang reels are group-chat, sitcom, map-journey x2; the last door reel (KG-2026-11-17-a) is 4 reels back, so door-arrivals fits every 2nd reel. Lead is Tanya (last reel led by Ishita). Chose the Secret Santa idea over the winter thermal one because a shawl and thermal cannot be drawn yet, so that twist would fail the mute test. Game plays 3 times, each through the guest's own trait with claim before reveal: Ruhi ordinary (her catchphrase 'kisi ko mat batana' then she tells Tanya to her face), Myra sillier (the new girl reads the name aloud because she does not know who Shruti is, and Shruti answers from the door), Shruti absurd (she never says a gift, she budgets her giftee on a calculator, 'Myra ke liye 150'). Twist is see-it: Tanya brags she alone keeps secrets, opens her chit and squeals the name. Button throws the hook line back at her. Endings tried: Tanya hides the chit and Ruhi reads it over her shoulder (weaker, Tanya not to blame), Ruhi drew Tanya so they swap gifts on the spot (sweet, no laugh), Tanya squeals and is sent out of her own door (kept). Every shot 8 words or fewer, hold 0.1, 67 words at pace 28, about 27 s."
  },
